#: ../../docs/tutorials/plugins/running_code_in_the_editor.rst:219
msgid "Editing variables"
msgstr ""

#: ../../docs/tutorials/plugins/running_code_in_the_editor.rst:221
msgid "Add and export a variable speed to the script. To update the speed and also reset the rotation angle add a setter ``set(new_speed)`` which is executed with the input from the inspector. Modify ``_process()`` to include the rotation speed."
msgstr ""

#: ../../docs/tutorials/plugins/running_code_in_the_editor.rst:271
msgid "Code from other nodes doesn't run in the editor. Your access to other nodes is limited. You can access the tree and nodes, and their default properties, but you can't access user variables. If you want to do so, other nodes have to run in the editor too."
msgstr ""

#: ../../docs/tutorials/plugins/running_code_in_the_editor.rst:277
msgid "Getting notified when arrays or dictionaries change"
msgstr ""

#: ../../docs/tutorials/plugins/running_code_in_the_editor.rst:279
msgid "You can use an Array or Dictionary as an ``@export`` variable. In a ``@tool`` script, you can react to any changes to that collection by using a setter. Normally, at runtime, such a setter is only called when you assign to the variable, but when you modify an Array or Dictionary in the inspector, the setter will also be called."
msgstr ""

